<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Portal</h1>
<p>Sphere: Summoning Sphere
Spell Tier: 3
Class: Sorcerer (guild level 120)
Mana: 40
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast portal &lt;someone or something&gt;
enter portal
look in portal
</pre>
<p>The caster raises their hands and cries 'Per infinitum conjuncto', and a 
glittering portal opens before them, with its twin beside the person or 
thing named, anywhere in the world. Type enter portal to step through. 
Each of the two portals takes one traveller and then vanishes, so the 
caster can go, and one person can come back. Look in a portal to see a 
blurred image of the far side first.
</p><p>The portals last for some minutes, at least two, longer the better your 
magic, brain and skill in the spell. Dispel magic closes one at once. 
Only players can step through.
</p><p>The far end resists: a player's own skill in the spell, a monster's in 
summoning, makes it harder to reach them. A poor casting does nothing; a 
very bad one opens a rift that flings you into the void and drains all 
your mana. Some places can't be reached by portal, or left by one. You 
must be standing. It is also found on scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
